# Vocabulary Data Rules

- Dual libraries: `library: "toefl" | "general"` with separate filters, stats, and progress.
- Normalize via adapters; keep original general fields; fill missing with null/defaults.
- Stable unique `id` per entry. Difficulty (CEFR) ≠ personal mastery (1–4).
- Write original definitions/examples. Cite provenance lightly (e.g. `awl-inspired`); never claim guaranteed TOEFL appearance.
- Prefer curated high-value academic words over bulk random advanced lists.
- Search must cover English, Arabic, definitions, synonyms, categories (Fuse.js).
---

# Mastery & SRS

- Ratings: Again / Hard / Good / Easy stored per word per library in IndexedDB.
- Schedule with transparent SM-2-style intervals; prioritize struggling words.
